{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The powered USB hub fits my history of adding computer connections through USB adapters and an expansion card; it could help me connect those accessories, although ten ports may exceed my needs.",
    "The USB extension cables relate to positioning my existing adapters, and the wired earbuds relate to my previous headset, though neither gives me a reason to buy without a specific need."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Echo speakers and Fire TV devices introduce home audio and streaming needs that my computer-accessory purchases do not establish.",
    "The drive enclosure and USB-B cable serve specific storage or printer connections I have not shown a need for; being useful computer accessories alone does not make them useful to me now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in electronics seems to have been stretched into an interest in smart speakers and streaming players.",
    "My USB purchases seem to have been treated as interest in anything with a USB connection, even when the connector or purpose differs from what I use."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My purchases repeatedly address concrete connection needs, such as adding WiFi, Ethernet, USB ports, or a display cable.",
    "I buy infrequently, so a related accessory needs to solve an actual problem before I would choose it; a past headset purchase does not by itself mean I need replacement audio gear."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my practical connection needs but stretched them too far into general electronics interest."
}"}
